     [38;5;255mI have the interfaces. Now let me write a full PP-OCR reader ([38;5;15m    
     [38;5;255mdetector + v3/v5 recognizers with CTC decode) and test it reads [38;5;15m  
     [38;5;255mthe Russian manga text verbatim. This is the "sees text + reads [38;5;15m  
     [38;5;255mit as it is" piece.[38;5;15m                                               
                                                                       
     [38;5;255mThe pipeline:[38;5;15m                                                     
                                                                       
     [38;5;216m1. [38;5;255mDetector: resize image to 736, normalize, run → probability [38;5;15m   
        [38;5;255mmap → threshold → find contours → get text boxes.[38;5;15m              
     [38;5;216m2. [38;5;255mFor each box: crop, resize to 48x320, normalize, run rec → [38;5;15m    
        [38;5;255mCTC greedy decode with dict → text.[38;5;15m                            
     [38;5;216m3. [38;5;255mSort boxes, output lines.[38;5;15m                                      
                                                                       
     [38;5;255mThis is standard PaddleOCR inference. Let me implement it [38;5;15m        
     [38;5;255mcarefully.[38;5;15m                                                        
                                                                       
